 555:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****     /* --- Reference input enable ---
 556:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      *
 557:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * The datasheet is explicit that all PLL reference inputs are OFF by
 558:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * default and that either a differential or a single-ended reference
 559:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * must be specifically enabled. Without this the PFD sees nothing and
 560:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * the PLL can never lock, even though every other register is correct.
 561:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      *
 562:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * PLL7 (0x01C) controls the reference input buffers and selection.
 563:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * AD9518_REF_INPUT_CFG is defined in ad9518.h so it can be adjusted for
 564:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * a differential versus single-ended reference without touching this
 565:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****      * function. Verify the bit assignment against Table 44 of your
