 667:Core/Src/ad9518.c **** /*
 668:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * Brute-force the reference input configuration until the PLL locks.
 669:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  *
 670:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * Register 0x01C selects and powers the reference input buffers, and its
 671:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * bit assignments were revised between datasheet revisions, so a value
 672:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * copied from an application note or an older driver may be wrong for the
 673:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * silicon actually fitted. Rather than trust one value, try them and let
 674:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * the digital lock detect decide.
 675:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  *
 676:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * Register 0x018[7] is also swept: for a single-ended AC-coupled reference
 677:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * it shifts the input bias point down ~140 mV to stop the input buffer
 678:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * chattering when the reference is slow or missing. It matters for some
 679:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * reference drivers and not others.
 680:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  *
ARM GAS  /var/folders/0g/t37nqzqx51l7sfxbqc44l9hw0000gn/T//ccBBrdod.s 			page 80


 681:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * Assumes the PLL counters, routing and channel dividers are already
 682:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * programmed - call this after ad9518_apply(). Returns 0 on lock with the
 683:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  * working values left in place, -1 if nothing locked.
 684:Core/Src/ad9518.c ****  */
